and evidence
Record source, build definition, toolchain, dependencies, runner image, identity, outputs, logs, and provenance. Protect the control plane, worker images, caches, registries, and logs as supply-chain assets. Architecture and Operating Decisions
Never expose release or production credentials to forked or untrusted code.
Keep signing independent from general build execution.
Pin third-party actions, plugins, images, and toolchains.
Restrict metadata services, container socket, host mounts, and privileged execution.
Test runner compromise, cache poisoning, credential misuse, and clean rebuild. Reference Configuration or Command Pattern
trust_tiers:
pr-validation: {secrets: none, network: restricted, runner: ephemeral}
protected-build: {identity: short-lived, registry: write-staging}
release: {approval: required, provenance: required}
signing: {artifact_input: digest-only, key_access: isolated}
production-deploy: {environment: protected, identity: scoped}
Production Readiness Checklist
☐ Ownership, trust boundaries, identities, inputs, outputs, and evidence are documented.
☐ Normal, negative, degraded, rollback, and recovery paths are tested.
